FerrionOS change to the upstream bootloader (MIT license, kept), applied after ferrion-edid-gop-mode.patch, made against upstream commit f3d9261b5fc81418c259c5059f46ee7087e86ed8:
- extend src/edid.rs to decode CTA-861 Video Data Block short video descriptors (progressive VICs 1-219, bounded by MAX_CTA_DATA_BLOCKS=32 and MAX_CTA_VICS=31), compute exact refresh rates in millihertz using u64 arithmetic across base/CTA DTDs, CTA VICs, and DisplayID Type I/VII timings, and return a bounded mode list (MAX_EDID_MODES=64) with warning on truncation;
- tighten choose_video_mode in src/main.rs to exact, exact aspect <= preferred, 1%-tolerance aspect <= preferred (ASPECT_TOLERANCE_NUM=1, ASPECT_TOLERANCE_DEN=100 in u64), largest mode that fits within the panel (w <= pw and h <= ph), and largest overall only when nothing fits;
- log the preferred timing's exact refresh rate and note that GOP sets size only.

